  "definition": "A barbiturate is a class of drugs that slows activity in the central nervous system. It works mainly by enhancing GABA-A receptor effects, which reduces nerve-cell signaling and can lead to sedation, sleep, anesthesia, coma, and reduced seizure activity.",
